# Example lane.env for a Pixel 8a (Tensor G3, Mali-G715, 8 GB, Android 16): the same app and plans as an S26 lane,
# another phone. Copy it next to a lane's plans as <lane>/device/lane.env, or keep the lane's file and write a small one
# that sets SERIAL / HOLD / DEVICE / RESULTS_DIR and then sources it (every value is ${VAR:-...}, so the first one set
# wins), and fill in the app's settings.
# What the Pixel is for: GPU and CPU legs (gates, form comparisons, the host loop and the measurement app's own
# checks), to narrow the candidates and to catch failures early. Not for NPU legs (LiteRT's NPU support for this phone
# is early access only) and not for card numbers: a Pixel PASS does not stand in for an S26 PASS (GPU ops and fp16
# behaviour differ between Mali and Adreno).
# The GPU (README "GPU reads"): the chains find the Mali driver at /sys/class/misc/mali0/device (no /sys/class/kgsl
# here). The shell user reads cur_freq (kHz, 150000 at idle), hint_min_freq, dvfs_period, capacity_headroom,
# dma_buf_gpu_mem and total_gpu_mem there, but not max_freq, min_freq, scaling_max_freq, hint_max_freq, governor,
# power_policy, available_frequencies, gpu_top, clock_info or dvfs_table (permission denied), nor
# /sys/class/devfreq/*/cur_freq or /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/type. The GPU's thermal cap is its GPU cooling
# device in `dumpsys thermalservice` (mType 3: thermal-gpufreq-0; the CPU's, mType 2: thermal-cpufreq-0/1/2; the five
# devices of other types are left out), its temperature the sensor G3D, the skin sensor VIRTUAL-SKIN. The ready gate's
# clean = thermal status 0, no CPU cap, gpu_cooling (thermal-gpufreq-0) at 0. Gate legs are the tested use here; check
# that definition against the GPU clock on the phone before planning timing legs.

LANE=${LANE:-example}
DEVICE=${DEVICE:-p8a}
PKG=${PKG:-com.example.gate}
STAGE=${STAGE:-/data/local/tmp/example_gate}
SERIAL=${SERIAL:?set SERIAL to the adb serial of the phone}
# one hold file per phone (the S26 keeps .device_hold): a Pixel run never blocks an S26 run
HOLD=${HOLD:-$CA/.device_hold.pixel8a}
GRAPH_DIR=${GRAPH_DIR:-$LANE_DIR/out}
ROWS_DIR=${ROWS_DIR:-$LANE_DIR/device}
RESULTS_DIR=${RESULTS_DIR:-$LANE_DIR/results}
APK=${APK:-$LANE_DIR/device/app-debug.$ROUND.apk}
ACTIVITY=${ACTIVITY:-.GateActivity}
SIG_OF=${SIG_OF:-}
APP_INT_EXTRAS=${APP_INT_EXTRAS:-limit_rows:limit warmup rest_ms reps cool_ms keep_scores cpu_cache gpu_src_quant}
APP_OUTPUTS=${APP_OUTPUTS:-sel full:keep_scores}
APP_LOG_TAG=${APP_LOG_TAG:-EXAMPLE_GATE}
PY=${PY:-python3}
ADB=${ADB:-adb}
STANDIN=${STANDIN:-$PY $LANE_DIR/scripts/fake_runner.py}
# 8 GB of memory (the S26 has 12 GB): a GPU compile that took 5.5 GB on the S26 leaves little here
MEM_GUARD_KB=${MEM_GUARD_KB:-1500000}
